    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">African Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">This project supports securing Omo National Park as a legally gazetted protected area, strengthening elephant protection and building community relations. It will improve security and information on ivory trafficking and the maintenance of wildlife corridors in the greater Omo ecosystem, home to the largest remaining elephant population in Ethiopia. Activities include demarcation of park boundaries, anti-poaching and development of pilot community wildlife areas and information networks.</narrative>
